y do ye persecute me as God,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And are not satisfied with my flesh?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Oh that my words were now written!¦layout ‚¤textÙ$Oh that they were printed in a book!¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/That they were graven with an iron pen and lead¦layout ‚¤textµIn the rock for ever!¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#For I know that my redeemer liveth,¦layout ‚¤textÙ9And that he shall stand at the latter day upon the earth:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ1And though after my skin worms destroy this body,¦layout ‚¤textÙ Yet in my flesh shall I see God:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text¼Whom I shall see for myself,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And mine eyes shall behold, and not another;¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ&Though my reins be consumed within me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(But ye should say, Why persecute we him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Seeing the root of the matter is found in me?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textºBe ye afraid of the sword:¦layout ‚¤textÙ0For wrath bringeth the punishments of the sword,¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ%That ye may know there is a judgment.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse